[Music]  6 44 here on a wednesday morning we  welcome you back here to the program  metro sheriff joe lombardo joining us  now for our morning cup of joe's segment  sheriff lombardo thank you once again  for joining us here bright and early on  a wednesday morning how are you  good morning john so uh leading up to  sleep last night oh  no sleep is sleep is overrated uh who  needs it right  uh it was a very busy election night  obviously leading up to election night  we talked to some businesses here in the  valley there have been some  reports around the country about  concerns about the  effects of the election and potential  protesting violence  did you see anything around the valley  did metro have to deal with anything  last night  no surprisingly we didn't um i was  we were basing everything off what you  heard and what you just  described and we thought we were going  to have some concerns with the  anarchists um just disrupting the  polling locations but thankfully we  didn't we had a you know very  comprehensive plan put in place  in conjunction with the secretary of  state and the attorney general and we  ensured that we had  officers available in case we were  called and thankfully nothing happened  so  that gives me some pride and you know  our community and  people how they deal with the what's  going on in the nation  so but yet we still have a couple days  to go obviously because  decisions haven't been completely made  and hopefully um  it's not contested and which causes uh  us some concerns  um and going forward so we're gonna have  all the resources still in place  to deal with it for the next few days  until we can finalize the vote across  the nation and  people make a decision how they're going  to act aside from this  potential issue that business owners at  least some of them had had brought up  what kind of security did metro provide  at the polling locations to more than  120 of them around clark county  yeah that's a good question so there was  concerns that we were going to  be oppressive if we were present and  people could see us there staged at the  polling location so we made a point of  staying  out of people's view but able to respond  quickly if needed  and so it was mostly just a drive-by  type  mode that we were in just to be aware  present  and able to respond in a in a timely  manner so um  other than that that that's that's all  she wrote basically we had a  department operations center stood up  similar to what we do with new year's  eve so we have a lot of resources  um to bear if needed via a phone call a  quick phone call we can  bring all those resources to play and we  had you know  internally uh the detectives were all  outfitted in uniforms in case we needed  to respond  in a timely manner similar to what we do  with other major events like new year's  eve so  but thankfully they were just bored and  we didn't have to go to that  uh go that direction they were they were  the only ones who were bored yesterday i  think given what was going on  let's talk about another issue we've  been covering recently this horrible  murder up on the east side of the valley  the death of michelle weissman the woman  who was riding her bike  pushed off by someone who's in a passing  car that person  died we know the driver of that van has  been arrested  i guess first of all what is the latest  from metro's point of view with the case  and  have have detectives been able to  pinpoint at least a motive of why this  tragedy even happened  yes um as far as the motive i'll answer  that question first  no other than just being idiots um it's  it's  actu it's a very tragic event and my  condolences go out to the  miss weissman's family it was senseless  it was every word you could think of to  describe it  so the the unique piece on this is the  driver of the van  had just been recently uh released from  prison i believe four months earlier  for violent crime and for so obviously  the  reform at prison didn't occur with this  individual and and  they attempted to uh do the same  uh event they did with the bicyclists  with miss weissman prior to miss  weissman but they missed those  individuals and they continued down the  street uh  apparently saw miss weissman and and hit  her  in the back area and knocking her to the  ground which we know that she  eventually died from her injuries and  then the  individual that affected the um  was thrown from the car because of the  force against miss weissman and  he eventually died too and then we were  able to get the  driver of the van in custody um  you know it it was a weird event when  the officers first arrived they didn't  know exactly what had  taken place and thankfully they were  able to piece it together  in a short period of time and do what  they do  so um now just an absolutely tragic  situation on the east side of the valley  we will uh we'll follow that case and  others  we do appreciate you joining us this  morning sheriff if you at home have a  question for sheriff lombardo  you can submit it on our website  8newsnow.com find out if it's answered  every wednesday we'll catch up with the  sheriff again next week

